From: Dana Whitfield <dana.whitfield@hangs-gc.example>
To: Tax preparation <tax@finance-demo.example>
Subject: HANGS Construction Services 2026 Forms W-2
Date: Tue, 12 Jan 2027 10:20:00 -0800
Message-ID: <HGC-2026-W2@hangs-gc.example>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: multipart/mixed; boundary="=_HGC_2026_w2_request"

--=_HGC_2026_w2_request
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: quoted-printable

Hi,

Attached are the 2026 earnings by employee, the payroll ledger by pay run and=
 the 2026 company vehicle use log from our safety manager. Please prepare the=
 2026 Forms W-2 and the W-3 for us to review; we plan to e-file them with the=
 SSA and mail the employee copies by the deadline.

The earnings file is the final year-end export from the payroll system. The Q=
1 to Q3 Forms 941 are filed; the Q4 941 is prepared and we will file it toget=
her with the W-2s.

Two things I am not sure about. Alicia Castellano (E-1101) started on Decembe=
r 7 and has applied for her Social Security card; it has not arrived yet. And=
 I do not think payroll ever picked up the personal use of the two pickups in=
 the vehicle log.

Thanks,
Dana Whitfield
Controller, HANGS Construction Services LLC

--=_HGC_2026_w2_request
Content-Type: application/vnd.openxmlformats-officedocument.spreadsheetml.sheet
Content-Transfer-Encoding: base64
Content-Disposition: attachment; filename="2026 earnings by employee.xlsx"
MIME-Version: 1.0

